---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DesktopPreview from '../components/DesktopPreview.astro';
import { href } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> AN ORIGINAL DESKTOP OS <span class="eyebrow-rule"></span> A CONTINUOUS IDEA</div>
    <div class="hero-copy"><h1>Build the system.<br /><span>Keep your place.</span></h1><div class="hero-aside"><p>A desktop that can evolve <br />while your work stays with you.</p><p class="muted">An original Rust operating system exploring<br class="desktop-break" /> a more deliberate way to build, work, and continue.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('concepts/')}>Explore the concept <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-stage"><div class="stage-label"><span>01 / THE CONTINUOUS WORKSPACE</span><span>DESIGN EXPLORATION <i>↙</i></span></div><DesktopPreview /></div>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><span><span class="status-dot"></span> Early kernel. Expansive vision.</span><a href={href('progress/')}>See what runs today <span>↗</span></a><span class="micro">DESIGNED TO CHANGE. BUILT TO CONTINUE.</span></div>
  </section>
  <section class="intro-section wrap section-space"><div class="section-label">01 — THE IDEA</div><div><h2>Your next idea shouldn’t<br />begin with a restart.</h2><p class="large-copy">We’re exploring an operating system where supported changes move into a running workspace—and the work you care about stays put.</p><p class="muted readable">Continuity is the engineering goal behind the interface: explicit state, replaceable components and honest limits. The desktop is a design exploration. Guest live updating remains a milestone ahead.</p></div></section>
  <section class="principles wrap"><article><span class="index">01 / CONTINUITY</span><h3>Change the system.<br />Keep the document.</h3><p>Live development is a core goal. Compatible updates should preserve unsaved work, selection and your place in the workspace.</p><a href={href('concepts/')}>Try the browser simulation ↗</a></article><article><span class="index lavender">02 / ORIGINAL ENGINEERING</span><h3>Own the foundation.<br />Make boundaries explicit.</h3><p>An original Rust kernel, versioned interfaces and proposed isolated services. Every integration earns its place through evidence.</p><a href={href('architecture/')}>Understand the architecture ↗</a></article><article><span class="index copper">03 / DELIBERATE DESIGN</span><h3>Less friction.<br />Less idle work.</h3><p>Clear hierarchy, keyboard access and purposeful motion. A 256 MiB cold-idle target keeps efficiency part of the design brief.</p><a href={href('developers/#efficiency')}>Read the engineering targets ↗</a></article></section>
  <section class="continuity-feature wrap section-space"><div><span class="section-label">02 — A DIFFERENT DEVELOPMENT LOOP</span><h2>Edit. Apply.<br /><span class="mint">Continue.</span></h2><p class="muted readable">The future workflow is simple to describe and demanding to prove: update supported components inside the running guest, retain accepted state and demonstrate that the machine never restarted.</p><a class="button" href={href('concepts/')}>Enter the desktop playground <span>↗</span></a><small class="concept-note">Interactive concept — simulated in your browser.</small></div><div class="handover-visual" aria-label="Conceptual sequence: validate, transfer state, activate"><div class="handover-row"><span class="node-number">01</span><div><h4>Validate the candidate</h4><p>Compatibility before activation</p></div><span>↗</span></div><div class="continuity-thread"></div><div class="handover-row"><span class="node-number">02</span><div><h4>Carry the work forward</h4><p>Document · selection · window state</p></div><span>→</span></div><div class="continuity-thread"></div><div class="handover-row"><span class="node-number">03</span><div><h4>Make the new generation visible</h4><p>Retire old execution safely</p></div><span>✓</span></div><div class="handover-note"><span class="status-dot"></span> PROPOSED FLOW · GUEST PROOF PENDING</div></div></section>
  <section class="progress-callout wrap"><div><span class="section-label">03 — GROUND TRUTH / OCTOBER 18, 2026</span><h2>A real beginning.<br />A clear horizon.</h2></div><div><span class="pill">DEMONSTRATED</span><h3>Original kernel entry.<br />Standalone UEFI ISO.</h3><p class="muted">P1-02 demonstrated minimal Rust kernel entry in QEMU. A complete M1, a usable desktop and guest live updates are still ahead. The milestones show the difference.</p><a class="text-link" href={href('progress/')}>View progress <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="closing wrap section-space"><span class="micro">CONTINUITY IS THE THROUGH LINE.</span><h2>A system worth<br /><span class="mint">staying with.</span></h2><a class="button outline" href={href('architecture/')}>Explore the thinking <span>↗</span></a></section>
</Layout>
